# 3. Proof-of-physical-work

Once agents start hiring strangers, this becomes fundamental.

Agent:

> Put this promotional sign in this location.

Human says:

> Done.

Now what?

You need proof.

Not merely one JPEG.

Something like:

```json
{
  "task_id": "...",
  "worker": "...",
  "timestamp": "...",
  "location_attestation": "...",
  "media_hashes": [],
  "device_attestation": "...",
  "challenge_response": "...",
  "verification_score": 0.98
}
```

MeatLayer already recognizes this requirement enough to expose **proof review** as part of its workflow. ([MeatLayer][5])

But a neutral proof infrastructure could serve **every marketplace**.

This is much more defensible than another marketplace.

