# 11. Work receipts

This could become its own protocol/API.

Every task produces:

```json
{
  "task": "...",
  "principal": "...",
  "executor": "...",
  "requested_at": "...",
  "completed_at": "...",
  "price": "...",
  "evidence": [],
  "verifier": "...",
  "result_hash": "...",
  "accepted": true
}
```

Then workers/agents accumulate **provable histories**.

This addresses a problem in both agent reputation and human reputation:

> Don't tell me you're good. Show me the signed history of things you actually accomplished.

There is current research converging on this exact direction: EpochX models humans and agents as peer participants where tasks are claimed, delivered, verified and settled, and completed work leaves reusable artifacts and execution traces. ([arXiv][7])

That is very close to your thinking.

